ready: 1
kind: rule
id: consolidation.rule.replay
display_id: RULE-CONSOLIDATION-REPLAY
module: consolidation
title: Which episodes a sleep run replays
summary: >-
  Explicit requests to remember replay first, then episodes in order of salience times need, up to the
  per-run cap; routine episodes only reinforce.
owner: crates/kernle-core/src/consolidation/replay.rs::select
inputs:
- name: pending episode
  source: Salience, label, and embedding of each pending episode
  source_kind: stored
- name: explicit request
  source: Whether the episode holds an explicit request to remember
  source_kind: stored
- name: recent episodes
  source: The stack's episodes from the last 30 days
  source_kind: stored
constants:
- consolidation.const.replay-cap
- consolidation.const.replay-min-salience
- consolidation.const.reinforce-similarity
calculations:
- name: need
  expr: >-
    0.5 + 0.5 × min(1, related sessions in 30 days ÷ 5), where a related session has an episode with cosine
    at least 0.6 to this one
- name: priority
  expr: salience × need
decision:
  nodes:
  - id: in
    node_kind: input
    text: One pending episode
  - id: explicit
    node_kind: decision
    text: Does it hold an explicit request to remember?
  - id: routine
    node_kind: decision
    text: Is it labeled boredom, or below the replay salience?
  - id: rank
    node_kind: calc
    text: Rank by salience times need
  - id: cap
    node_kind: decision
    text: Within the per-run cap?
  - id: replay
    node_kind: outcome
    text: Replay for extraction
  - id: reinforce
    node_kind: outcome
    text: Reinforce the closest existing memory if it is close enough, otherwise skip
  - id: wait
    node_kind: outcome
    text: Stay pending for the next run
  edges:
  - from: in
    to: explicit
  - from: explicit
    to: cap
    label: Yes, ranked first
  - from: explicit
    to: routine
    label: 'No'
  - from: routine
    to: reinforce
    label: 'Yes'
  - from: routine
    to: rank
    label: 'No'
  - from: rank
    to: cap
  - from: cap
    to: replay
    label: 'Yes'
  - from: cap
    to: wait
    label: 'No'
rationale: >-
  Priority multiplies salience by need, as in prioritized replay: an experience is worth consolidating
  when it mattered and when similar situations keep coming up. Explicit requests always replay because
  skipping a request that scored low would break trust in remembering.
